            "topic": "miscellaneous",
            "heading": "Treatment of Departures From Guam",
            "text": "Treatment of Departures From GuamPub. L. 99–505, § 2, Oct. 21, 1986, 100 Stat. 1806, provided that: “In the administration of section 101(a)(15)(D)(ii) of the Immigration and Nationality Act [8 U.S.C. 1101(a)(15)(D)(ii)] (added by the amendment made by section 1 of this Act), an alien crewman shall be considered to have departed from Guam after leaving the territorial waters of Guam, without regard to whether the alien arrives in a foreign state before returning to Guam.”",
