            "topic": "miscellaneous",
            "heading": "VERIFICATION OF ELIGIBILITY FOR BENEFITS",
            "text": "VERIFICATION OF ELIGIBILITY FOR BENEFITSThe law denies most government benefits to illegal aliens. The government has a duty to assure that taxpayer-supported public assistance programs are not abused. As with work authorization, enforcement of eligibility requirements relies upon a credible system of verification. The INS, working with the White House Interagency Working Group on Immigration as appropriate, shall review means of improving the existing benefits verification program. In addition, we will seek new mechanisms—including increased penalties for false information used to qualify for benefits—to protect the integrity of public programs.",
