              "label": "Initial admission",
              "value": "Up to 3 years — historical H-1C classification; unavailable since December 20, 2009",
              "excerpt": "(ii) Extension periods—(A) H-1C extension of stay. The maximum period of admission for an H-1C alien is 3 years. An H-1C alien who was initially admitted to the United States for less than 3 years may receive an extension of stay up to the third anniversary date of his or her initial admission. An H-1C nonimmigrant may not receive an extension of stay beyond the third anniversary date of his or her initial admission to the United States.",
