              "key": "initial_admission",
              "label": "Initial admission",
              "value": "Necessary period for the event or activity, up to 3 years",
              "excerpt": "(iii) Validity—(A) O-1 petition. An approved petition for an alien classified under section 101(a)(15)(O)(i) of the Act shall be valid for a period of time determined by the Director to be necessary to accomplish the event or activity, not to exceed 3 years.\n\n(B) O-2 petition. An approved petition for an alien classified under section 101(a)(15)(O)(ii) of the Act shall be valid for a period of time determined to be necessary to assist the O-1 alien to accomplish the event or activity, not to exceed 3 years.",
              "challengeText": "Necessary period for the event or activity, up to 3 years",
              "source": {
                "resource": "Electronic Code of Federal Regulations",
                "locator": "8 CFR 214.2(o)(6)(iii)(A)-(B)",
                "url": "https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-8/section-214.2",
                "captureDate": "2026-07-29",
                "supportingExcerpt": "(iii) Validity—(A) O-1 petition. An approved petition for an alien classified under section 101(a)(15)(O)(i) of the Act shall be valid for a period of time determined by the Director to be necessary to accomplish the event or activity, not to exceed 3 years.\n\n(B) O-2 petition. An approved petition for an alien classified under section 101(a)(15)(O)(ii) of the Act shall be valid for a period of time determined to be necessary to assist the O-1 alien to accomplish the event or activity, not to exceed 3 years."
              },
